<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=utf-8">
    <title>
      Advisories
    </title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="lfs.css">
    <link rel="icon" href="favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
  </head>
  <body>
    <h1>
      Advisories
    </h1>
    <h2>
      Introduction
    </h2>
    <p>
      This site hosts advisories for a collection of LFS books, which are
      generated from XML. This site doesn't host the XML, but instead HTML
      that has been transformed via XSLT from the XML.
    </p>
    <p>
      Currently supported books:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <b>Gaming Linux From Scratch</b>
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Supplemental Linux From Scratch</b>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The XML the advisories are written in is hosted <a href=
      "https://github.com/glfs-book/advisories">here</a>. The XML is licensed
      under the MIT license. You may transform and pull the XML how you wish.
    </p>
    <h2>
      Reading the HTML
    </h2>
    <p>
      The following links contain advisories for each supported book:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="glfs.html">GLFS Advisories</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="slfs.html">SLFS Advisories</a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </body>
</html>
